		(property "BOM Comments" "Unit cost = fuse est. 0.40 + holder est. 3.00 (holder price unverified). ATO/ATC 257: 32 VDC, 1000 A interrupting at 32 VDC, ISO 8820-3 / SAE J1284; melting I2t about 340 A2s (15 A, Littelfuse catalog). 0257015.L is obsolete; DigiKey lists 0287015.PXCN (ATOF) as direct substitute. Holder takes standard ATO/ATC blade fuses; 22.5 A continuous / 30 A max per the Littelfuse FLR datasheet; 32 V fuse system; either exceeds F1. Buy spare fuses. See Fuse notes in bom.md"
